From: DBY-W09 contributors <dby-w09@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] tty: serial: qcom-geni: limit system-sleep votes to active state

Serdev clients can keep the controller runtime-active while suspended.
Apply the console ICC policy to all ports so those references cannot
retain sleep-set bandwidth. Preserve active and wake bandwidth and
restore the normal tag on resume. Protocol and wake IRQ handling stay
with the existing serial and serdev drivers.

Signed-off-by: DBY-W09 contributors <dby-w09@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c
@@ -1983,14 +1983,10 @@
 	struct uart_port *uport = &port->uport;
 	struct qcom_geni_private_data *private_data = uport->private_data;
 
-	/*
-	 * This is done so we can hit the lowest possible state in suspend
-	 * even with no_console_suspend
-	 */
-	if (uart_console(uport)) {
-		geni_icc_set_tag(&port->se, QCOM_ICC_TAG_ACTIVE_ONLY);
-		geni_icc_set_bw(&port->se);
-	}
+	/* Serdev ports may retain runtime PM references across system sleep. */
+	geni_icc_set_tag(&port->se, QCOM_ICC_TAG_ACTIVE_ONLY);
+	geni_icc_set_bw(&port->se);
+
 	return uart_suspend_port(private_data->drv, uport);
 }
 
@@ -2002,10 +1998,8 @@
 	struct qcom_geni_private_data *private_data = uport->private_data;
 
 	ret = uart_resume_port(private_data->drv, uport);
-	if (uart_console(uport)) {
-		geni_icc_set_tag(&port->se, QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS);
-		geni_icc_set_bw(&port->se);
-	}
+	geni_icc_set_tag(&port->se, QCOM_ICC_TAG_ALWAYS);
+	geni_icc_set_bw(&port->se);
 	return ret;
 }
 
